          "type": "learn",
          "id": "c5-pressure-02",
          "title": "Double A-gap and cross dog",
          "body": "Two linebackers walk up into the A gaps beside the center, threatening to come straight through. In a cross dog, two linebackers cross paths as they blitz to confuse the blockers.",
          "concept": "a-gap-blitz"
        },
        {
          "type": "learn",
          "id": "c5-pressure-03",
          "title": "Overload and creeper",
          "body": "An overload sends more rushers to one side than it can block. A creeper (simulated pressure) rushes only four but from unexpected spots, dropping a lineman: pressure without giving up coverage.",
          "concept": "simulated-pressure"
        },
